{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "ts-config-service",
      "fault_kind": "database_call_slow",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) n, round(avg(duration)/1e6,0) avg_ms, round(min(duration)/1e6,0) min_ms, round(max(duration)/1e6,0) max_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-config-service' AND span_name IN ('SELECT Config','ConfigRepository.findByName','ConfigController.retrieve') GROUP BY 1,2",
          "claim": "In the incident, config's SELECT Config and findByName spans each take about 30s, against about 2ms normally."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, round(avg(duration)/1e6,1) avg_ms FROM normal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-config-service' AND attr_span_kind='Server' GROUP BY 1",
          "claim": "Normal-period config server spans average about 1.8ms, so the 30s latency is a regression."
        },
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT 'ab' p, metric, round(avg(value),3) avg_v FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE service_name='ts-config-service' AND metric IN ('container.cpu.usage','container.memory.usage') GROUP BY 1,2 UNION ALL SELECT 'norm', metric, round(avg(value),3) FROM normal_metrics WHERE service_name='ts-config-service' AND metric IN ('container.cpu.usage','container.memory.usage') GROUP BY 1,2",
          "claim": "Config container CPU and memory stay at normal levels, so the slowdown is not resource saturation."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "ts-config-service",
      "to": "ts-seat-service",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT p.service_name parent_svc, c.service_name child_svc, count(*) n, round(avg(p.duration)/1e6,0) parent_ms, round(avg(c.duration)/1e6,0) child_ms FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces p ON c.parent_span_id = p.span_id AND c.trace_id=p.trace_id WHERE p.service_name='ts-seat-service' AND c.service_name='ts-config-service' GROUP BY 1,2",
          "claim": "Seat's calls to config average about 30s child time, and seat's own requests take about 60s."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "from": "ts-seat-service",
      "to": "ts-travel-service",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT p.service_name parent_svc, c.service_name child_svc, count(*) n, round(avg(p.duration)/1e6,0) parent_ms, round(avg(c.duration)/1e6,0) child_ms FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces p ON c.parent_span_id = p.span_id AND c.trace_id=p.trace_id WHERE p.service_name='ts-travel-service' AND c.service_name='ts-seat-service' GROUP BY 1,2",
          "claim": "Travel's calls to seat take about 60s, matching seat's slow left-tickets handling."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "from": "ts-seat-service",
      "to": "ts-travel2-service",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT p.service_name parent_svc, c.service_name child_svc, count(*) n, round(avg(p.duration)/1e6,0) parent_ms, round(avg(c.duration)/1e6,0) child_ms FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces p ON c.parent_span_id = p.span_id AND c.trace_id=p.trace_id WHERE p.service_name='ts-travel2-service' AND c.service_name='ts-seat-service' GROUP BY 1,2",
          "claim": "Travel2's calls to seat take about 60s, so travel2 inherits seat's latency."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "from": "ts-travel-service",
      "to": "ts-route-plan-service",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT p.service_name parent_svc, c.service_name child_svc, count(*) n, round(avg(p.duration)/1e6,0) parent_ms, round(avg(c.duration)/1e6,0) child_ms FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces p ON c.parent_span_id = p.span_id AND c.trace_id=p.trace_id WHERE p.service_name='ts-route-plan-service' AND c.service_name='ts-travel-service' GROUP BY 1,2",
          "claim": "Route-plan's calls into travel take about 38s, close to travel's own slow time."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "from": "ts-travel2-service",
      "to": "ts-route-plan-service",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT p.service_name parent_svc, c.service_name child_svc, count(*) n, round(avg(p.duration)/1e6,0) parent_ms, round(avg(c.duration)/1e6,0) child_ms FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces p ON c.parent_span_id = p.span_id AND c.trace_id=p.trace_id WHERE p.service_name='ts-route-plan-service' AND c.service_name='ts-travel2-service' GROUP BY 1,2",
          "claim": "Route-plan's calls into travel2 take about 36s, so travel2 latency also reaches route-plan."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "from": "ts-route-plan-service",
      "to": "ts-travel-plan-service",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT p.service_name parent_svc, c.service_name child_svc, count(*) n, round(avg(p.duration)/1e6,0) parent_ms, round(avg(c.duration)/1e6,0) child_ms FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces p ON c.parent_span_id = p.span_id AND c.trace_id=p.trace_id WHERE p.service_name='ts-travel-plan-service' AND c.service_name='ts-route-plan-service' GROUP BY 1,2",
          "claim": "Travel-plan's calls into route-plan take about 60s, so route-plan latency reaches travel-plan."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "from": "ts-travel-plan-service",
      "to": "ts-ui-dashboard",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT p.service_name parent_svc, c.service_name child_svc, count(*) n, round(avg(p.duration)/1e6,0) parent_ms, round(avg(c.duration)/1e6,0) child_ms FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces p ON c.parent_span_id = p.span_id AND c.trace_id=p.trace_id WHERE p.service_name='ts-ui-dashboard' AND c.service_name='ts-travel-plan-service' GROUP BY 1,2",
          "claim": "UI dashboard's calls to travel-plan average about 60s child time, so the user-facing dashboard shows the delay."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "from": "ts-travel-service",
      "to": "ts-ui-dashboard",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT p.service_name parent_svc, c.service_name child_svc, count(*) n, round(avg(p.duration)/1e6,0) parent_ms, round(avg(c.duration)/1e6,0) child_ms FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces p ON c.parent_span_id = p.span_id AND c.trace_id=p.trace_id WHERE p.service_name='ts-ui-dashboard' AND c.service_name='ts-travel-service' GROUP BY 1,2",
          "claim": "UI dashboard's calls to travel average about 24s child time, so travel's slowness reaches the user-facing dashboard directly."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

**Summary:** The user-visible degradation is in `ts-ui-dashboard` and the trip-query endpoints. The root cause is a single database-level fault in `ts-config-service`: its `SELECT Config` call takes about 30s instead of about 2ms. CPU and memory are normal and the config↔mysql network flows show no retransmit or drop signal, so this is classed as `database_call_slow`. No spans or logs error out; the failure appears as latency. The slowdown propagates through `ts-seat-service`, which calls config on every left-tickets query. It then reaches `ts-travel-service` and `ts-travel2-service`, then `ts-route-plan-service`, then `ts-travel-plan-service`, and finally the dashboard.

Other services that look changed (`ts-travel*`, `ts-route-plan`, `ts-travel-plan`) are downstream victims with no fault of their own. Some services show far fewer spans in the incident window (for example the food and contacts services), but that tracks which flows the load generator exercised rather than a failure, so I did not name them.
